# oh103, the storm-watcher (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh103
revision 1
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_ingram_ashleaf
written_by claude
title the storm-watcher
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=woodcutter temper=nervy
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sleeps_badly_before_storms
likes fried_fish evening_line old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes drizzle haggling
fears a_tree_on_the_roof_in_the_night the_brook_pool_freezing_early
hopes a_road_off_the_edge_of_my_map
topics weather +0.5 pastimes +0.3 friends +0.3 travel +0.2 food +0.2 newcomer -0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=company gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# drags logs at the cut and frets at the sky: warm and anxious, quick to ask how you are and slow to believe the answer, awake half the night before any storm, and happiest of an evening with a line in the brook pool and an old map spread on the knees.

words
oath! = Mercy on the leaves | Oh, bark and bother
saying! = Better a roof checked twice than once | Every map's wrong somewhere, and so am I
storm = a storm | a storm coming over the tops
sky = the sky | the sky over the oaks
map = the old map | a map with every road astray
oaks = the oaks | the big oaks
gate = the gate | the town gate
forest = the forest | the oakwood
carter = the carter | the South Road carter
maps = my old maps | the maps in the chest
fishline = my line | a line in the brook
pool = the brook pool | the pool under the alders
pan = a trout in the pan with butter | fried fish, butter and all
halfrain = this half-rain | a drip that never commits
rime = a white morning | rime on every twig
haggle = haggling | haggling at the stall
logs = the logs | the trimmed logs
skid = the skid | the log skid
roof = the roof | our roof
sawmill = the sawmill | the mill saw
city = the city | Ridgemere

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : #city.capitalize#? Smoke and strangers, and nobody to ask how you slept. I'd be lost in a day, even with #map#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A town the size of #here.town# can feed its own. I'd lie awake if one of us went without.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : A wolf in drink says things that can't be unsaid. I worry enough about the things I say sober.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I drag #logs# all the week and the counters still want more for a loaf than I've got. I hate #haggle# for it, too.
opinion @1 road against 1 : The South Road's no place for a wolf these days. #maps.capitalize# are safer; they've no robbers on them.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new face at #gate# keeps me up till I've learned whose it is. I'd sooner #gate# stayed quiet.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. Are you lost? You look a bit lost. | #greet#. You've come a long way, I'd guess. Sit down.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=woodcutter] : #greet#. Mind #skid#; the logs run. | #greet#. Stand back, #address#, these are heavy.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. You're up early. I hope you slept. | #greet#, #address#. Cold one, this morning.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. I was just off to #pool#. | #greet#. Late to be out, #address#. I hope all's well.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are, #address#. I was starting to worry. | Come in, come in. There's food if you've not eaten, #address#.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'm glad. I'd wondered how you were getting on. | #welcome_back#, #address#. I hope it's been a quiet day.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. #good.capitalize# to see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I was hoping you'd come by, #address#. | #greet#. Oh, it's you. Sit, sit.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=woodcutter] : #greet#. Give me a moment with #logs#. | #greet#. Stand clear of #skid# and I'm all yours.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Mind how you go. | #farewell#, #address#. Take care, now.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the path; the roots are bad in the dark. | #farewell#. Get home before the weather, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And you, #address#. Look after yourself.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. Is everyone all right? | Oh, that's news. I hope nobody's hurt, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard a whisper. | That's new to me, #address#. When was this?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It kept me up half the night. | I'd heard. I've been turning it over since, #address#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I hope it's not true. | Are you sure, #address#? I'd hate to worry for nothing.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, no. #pity#. | That's #bad#. I'll not sleep for thinking of it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Oh, I'm glad. | That's #good#, #address#. Something to feel easy about.
line @1 answer.how : Tired. I slept #bad#. The sky's been heavy. | Well enough, #address#. Better for asking.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #logs.capitalize# won't drag themselves. | Run off my paws, #address#. Ask me at dusk.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Truly? | How are you keeping, #address#? Sleeping well?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit with me a while. | Oh, #address#. I'm sorry. Is there anything I can do?
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It'll be all right. | It'll come right, #address#. I'll do the fretting; you rest.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I'd better not. #logs.capitalize# are behind and I'd fret all day. | I'm sorry, #address#, I can't. I've promised the day already, and I'd only worry.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Truly, it's fine. | That's all right, #address#. Another time.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That's #very# kind of you. | #thanks#, #address#. I'll remember that.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. I'd do it again tomorrow. | Oh, it was nothing, #address#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes self.job=woodcutter] : Well. #logs.capitalize# are waiting. | #excuse#. They'll want me at #skid#.
line @2 preclose : #preclose#. | Well. I should look at #roof# before dark, #address#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. Mind yourself. | Of course. Take care, #address#.
line @1 ack : Mm. | Mm, #address#. I see.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: check your roof before the weather, not after. | Take a staff on the forest paths. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Don't go out #gate# alone, #address#. There's talk of #bandits#. | Please, stay off the road a while. I'd not sleep, knowing.
scene before_storm
when topic=weather|day here.weather=overcast
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : There's #storm# in that sky. I lay awake half the night with it pressing on my ears. | I didn't sleep a wink. I always know when #storm#'s on the way. | Look how still #oaks# are. They're waiting for something.
b : It might pass over. | Bad night, then? | Maybe it's nothing.
a : It might. I'll not sleep till it does, all the same. | #bad#. I counted the beams till dawn. | Maybe. But they don't hold still for nothing, #address#.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene storm_night
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.worry / sympathise / reassure
tone serious / serious / even
a : Hear that wind in the tops? I've been up twice already to look at #roof#. | A branch came down by #gate#. I knew it would. I said so, didn't I? | #storm.capitalize#, and every oak in the forest groaning. I can't settle.
b : The roof will hold. | You did say. | Sit, then. I'll sit with you.
a : I know it will. I've checked it. I'll check it again. | I take no joy in it. #hedge#, I'd rather be wrong for once. | #thanks#. It's better with somebody else awake.

scene roof_checked
when topic=home|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I was up on #roof# again this morning, checking the shingles. | I keep a ladder by the door, #address#. Just in case. | I tie the shutters down every night now, whatever #sky# says.
b : Was anything loose? | In case of what? | Every night?
a : One. One shingle, and I'd have lain awake on it for a week. #saying#. | In case of anything. A wind, a branch, a cat. It's never wasted. | Every night. You can laugh, #address#. I'll still sleep better.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_fair#

scene the_maps
when topic=pastimes|travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've #map# from a carter. It has the South Road going straight through the brook pool. | #maps.capitalize# are all wrong, every one. That's what I like about them. | Somebody drew a town on #map# that's never been there. I wonder who lived in it.
b : Straight through? | Why like them wrong? | Who'd draw a town that isn't there?
a : Straight through. Whoever drew it never got their feet wet. | A wrong map's a puzzle. A right one's only a road. | Somebody hopeful, I think. I'd like to have met them.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_lovely#

scene map_dreams
when topic=dreams|travel
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #vent#: I've a few coins put by. I'll not say what for. It's on one of #maps#, somewhere. | I dream of walking off the edge of #map#, just to see what's there. | Some nights I spread out #maps# and pick a road. I never walk it. But I pick it.
b : I'll not ask. | What do you think is there? | Maybe one day.
a : #thanks#. I'd only fret if I said it aloud. | More of #oaks#, probably. I'd like to see them anyway. | Maybe. #someday#, when #sky#'s clear for a week.

scene evening_fishing
when topic=pastimes here.time=dusk self.likes=evening_line
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'm off to put #fishline# in #pool#. It's the only hour my head goes quiet. | Nothing calms me like #fishline# at dusk. Even when nothing bites. | Two trout last evening, and one I let go because it looked so surprised.
b : Quiet's good. | Even with nothing? | You let one go?
a : It is. The water doesn't ask me anything. | Especially then. Then there's nothing to worry over. | It had a whole evening ahead of it, #address#. I'd not take that from anything.

scene fish_supper
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pan.capitalize#. That's my idea of a good supper. | The smell of fish in butter. I'd come home from anywhere for that. | Fresh from #pool# to the pan inside an hour. You can taste the difference.
b : Sounds good. | From anywhere? | Can you?
a : It is. Come by, #address#, if I've two. | Even off the edge of #map#. I'd smell it. | You can. Ask any wolf who's had it the other way.

scene rime_morning
when topic=weather|season here.time=dawn here.weather=clear here.season=winter|autumn self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #rime.capitalize#. The whole cut's gone white overnight. I love a morning like this. | Clear and cold, and every branch furred white. #forest.capitalize# looks new. | Hear that? Nothing. A cold still morning, and #sky# empty. I slept like a log.
b : It's cold, though. | It does look new. | You slept?
a : Cold, and honest. You know where you are with a cold, clear sky. | New as the first morning. I stood and looked till my paws went numb. | Like a felled log. No storm in a sky like this, #address#.

scene half_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|fog self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #halfrain.capitalize#. Not rain enough to stop work, and not fine enough to enjoy. | It's been dripping since dawn and never once properly raining. I can't bear it. | Wet fur all day, and not even a good downpour to show for it.
b : At least it's not a storm. | It'll make its mind up. | Miserable, isn't it.
a : There's that. I'll be thankful for a small wet thing, then. | I hope so. I'd rather #storm#, almost. Almost. | Miserable. And nothing bites at #pool# in it, either.

scene the_skid
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter self.working=yes
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : I drag #logs# down #skid# to the carts. If one runs, I want everyone clear. | Grease on #skid# again. A log went down it this morning like a startled boar. | I check every chain twice before a log moves. They laugh at me for it.
b : Nobody's been hurt? | A boar! | Better safe.
a : Not on my skid, and not while I'm watching. #saying#. | A boar with no brakes, #address#. I shouted myself hoarse. | Better safe, and better laughed at than carried home.

scene mill_scream
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=oakhaven self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #sawmill.capitalize#'s been screaming since dawn. Our logs, every one. | The joiners want oak, oak and more oak. I've dragged till my shoulders are #tired#. | I like taking logs to #sawmill#. Then they're somebody else's worry.
b : Busy, then. | They always want oak. | Somebody else's?
a : #very# busy. Good for the purse, bad for the back. | Always. Oak's slow to grow and quick to sell. | The joiners' worry. I've enough of my own, #address#.

scene no_haggling
when topic=prices|work self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I went to buy a hook and came out with a quarrel. I can't stand #haggle#. | Every stall wants to argue. I pay what they ask and lose sleep over it. | #carter.capitalize# tried to talk me down on a load I'd not even offered to sell.
b : You have to haggle. | You should argue back. | Did you sell?
a : Then I'll pay more and sleep better. It's worth a copper. | I'd lie awake on the argument instead. I'd rather lose the copper. | No. I was so muddled I walked off with the load still on my back.

scene spouse_quiet
when topic=family|home self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
tone tender / even / even
a : #self.spouse# sleeps through any storm. I lie awake for the both of us. | I worry, and #self.spouse# doesn't. Between us, that's #very# near right. | I'd be lost without #self.spouse#. I don't say it often enough.
b : That's a good match. | It works, then. | You could say it now.
a : It is. Somebody in the house should get some sleep. | It works. I hold the worry; my #self.spouse_word# holds the rest. | I might. Tonight, maybe, if #sky#'s quiet.

scene the_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd go to with a worry, and come away lighter. | I'd trust #self.friend# with anything. Even #maps#. | When I've slept badly, #self.friend# knows by looking and doesn't ask. That's a friend.
b : That's worth a lot. | Even the maps? | That's rare.
a : More than coin, #address#. More than sleep, even. | Even those. From me, that's no small thing. | It is. I'm lucky in that, #address#, and I know it.

scene thin_weeks
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : It gets a little dearer every week and the pay doesn't follow. Nobody up at the big houses notices. | I lie awake doing sums now, as well as listening for storms. | We've cut the bread thinner #home#. Nobody's said it, but we have.
b : We'll manage. | That's no good for you. | Everyone's doing the same.
a : We will. #reassure#. I only wish I believed it at night. | No good at all. But the sums don't change for my lying awake. | I know. That's the worry of it, #address#. It's everyone.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : There's a stranger in town. I hope they're decent. I'll not sleep till I know. | New faces through #gate#. I'd like to know who before I lock up. | A traveller wanted directions to #sawmill#. I gave them, then fretted I'd said too much.
b : They're probably fine. | You'll find out soon. | It's only the way.
a : Probably. I'll worry until it's certainly, #address#. | I will. #here.town# is small; everyone's known in a week. | I know. I'll worry anyway, #address#. It's what I do.

scene gossip_fret
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : There's talk going round. I wish there wasn't. Somebody always gets hurt by #busybody# talk. | I heard a thing about someone, and now I can't look at them straight. I wish I hadn't. | I don't carry tales. I'd only lie awake wondering if I'd got it right.
b : Don't pass it on, then. | That's a weight to carry. | Wise.
a : I won't. It stops with me, and keeps me awake instead. | It is. I'll get over it. It's only talk, #address#. | Wise, or just #tired#. Either way, it stops with me.

scene faith_storm
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Every night I have a word with the Bright One. Mostly about #sky#. | I'm not much for chapel. But in #storm# I find I pray well enough. | My #mum# said the Bright One hears the anxious best. I've given plenty of practice.
b : The weather's a fair thing to pray for. | Storms do that. | That's a kind thought.
a : I'd think so. It's the thing I fret over most. | They do. I'm a better wolf in #storm#. More honest, anyway. | It was. It's kept me going, #address#.

story wrong_road [topic=travel|memories self.likes=old_maps self.age>=25]
  : Once I followed one of #maps# to find a short way to Larkfield. It showed a bridge.
  : There was no bridge. There'd never been a bridge. Only a river and a very wet wolf.
  ask : Would you have trusted it?
  b : No. Never trust a short way.
  b[old] : Once. Only once.
  : I still have that map. I've drawn the bridge in, so the next fool has it right.

story the_oak_on_the_roof [topic=memories|weather self.age>=30]
  : When I was young, a storm put a bough through #roof# of our old house.
  : It came down where I'd been sleeping an hour before. #mum.capitalize# had moved me, for no reason she could say.
  ask : Do you think something warned her?
  b : Something did, I'd say.
  b[old] : Mothers know. They always know.
  : I think so. I've slept badly before every storm since.

story the_surprised_trout [topic=pastimes|animals self.likes=evening_line]
  : I hooked a trout once so big I was sure it would pull me in.
  : I got it to the bank, and it looked up at me as though I'd insulted it.
  b : Did you keep it?
  : I let it go. A fish that fights that hard has earned #pool#.

rule @storm_worry
when concept=bark here.weather=overcast|storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mercy, look at that sky. | #storm.capitalize#. I knew it. I said so.

rule @skid_call
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=woodcutter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind #skid#! Log coming! | Stand clear, #address#, she's running!

rule @drip_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Rain, or don't. Make up your mind. | #halfrain.capitalize#. #annoyed#.

rule @dusk_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk self.likes=evening_line
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #pool.capitalize#'s calling. Just an hour. | Where did I put #fishline#?

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Are you all right? Can I help at all? | #greet#, #address#. Sit down. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I'd wondered how you were. What is it?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Please, gently. Tell me what's wrong and I'll help if I can.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=woodcutter] : I drag #logs# at the cut and send them down #skid# to the carts. And I check every chain twice. | Logging. Heavy work, and I fret over every log till it's safe at #sawmill#.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I worry, and of an evening I fish. That's me, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Quiet suits me fine. | Nothing, #address#. Quiet's the best news.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind how you go. | #farewell#, #address#. Look after yourself.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that old map you keep looking at? -> map
node map
say It's from a carter. Half the roads on it are wrong. It has a bridge where there's no bridge; I know, I looked.
mood warm
free
choice Why keep a wrong map? -> map_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node map_why
say A wrong map's a puzzle. Somebody hoped those roads were there. I like to think of the places they hoped for.
choice That's a nice thought. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
